{"name":"Coastal Dusk","hex":"#727b76","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coastal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to the coast; on or near the coast; longshore."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coastal"},{"term":"dusk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tending to darkness or blackness; moderately dark or black; dusky."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time after the sun has set but when the sky is still lit by sunlight; the evening twilight period.","A darkish colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast"},{"title":"Dusk","blocks":[{"text":"Dusk occurs at the darkest stage of twilight, or at the very end of astronomical twilight after sunset and just before nightfall. At predusk, during early to intermediate stages of twilight, enough light in the sky under clear conditions may occur to read outdoors without artificial illumination; however, at the end of civil twilight, such lighting is required to read outside. The term dusk usually refers to astronomical dusk, or the darkest part of twilight before night begins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg/330px-Landers_in_the_Mojave_Desert_at_dusk%2C_looking_west_from_Joshua_Tree%2C_California_USA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusk"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/1280px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Knights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rugged coastline of the West Coast Region of New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKnights_Point_-_Tasm%C3%A1nsk%C3%A9_mo%C5%99e_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/500px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/1280px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg/500px-Somalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Somalia has the longest coastline in Africa.[12]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASomalia_16.08.2009_08-30-13.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.